import json
R=[
("temptation-of-adam",7,1,"Eve offers a fruit to Adam, who reaches for it, with the tree of knowledge between them. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1550, and the muscled bodies show how he was influenced by Michelangelo."),
("the-land-of-cockaigne",4,0,"A farmer, a soldier and a scholar lie asleep and full of food under a tree, in a land where roast pigs run around with knives in their backs. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1567, and it is a funny picture of an imaginary land where nobody works."),
("venus-and-cupid-sustris",5,1,"The goddess Venus lies on a bed with her little son Cupid beside her. Lambert Sustris painted it in about 1550, and the soft landscape through the window is typical of Venice."),
("a-meat-stall-with-the-holy-family-giving-alms",4,0,"A big butcher's stall full of sausages, a pig's head and cuts of meat takes up the front, while in the back Mary, Joseph and the baby Jesus give a coin to a beggar. Pieter Aertsen painted it in 1551, and the food is the star."),
("the-egg-dance",4,0,"Villagers dance around eggs on the ground at a country party, in a cheerful, noisy scene. Pieter Aertsen painted it in 1552, and the dancers have to step between the eggs without breaking them."),
("portrait-of-mary-tudor",1,0,"A queen with a plain, tight-lipped face sits in a rich, red dress, with a rose in her hand. Antonis Mor painted Mary Tudor, queen of England, in 1554, for her husband Philip II of Spain."),
("self-portrait-anguissola",1,0,"A young woman in a dark dress holds a medallion with a monogram and looks out with a clear, direct gaze. Sofonisba Anguissola painted it in 1554, and she was one of the first women to become a famous painter in Europe."),
("portrait-of-the-artist-s-sisters-playing-chess",4,0,"Three sisters play chess, while a maid stands behind them, as one sister smiles at her own move. Sofonisba Anguissola painted her sisters in 1555, and it was one of the first group portraits that looked like a real family moment."),
("saint-george-and-the-dragon",5,0,"A young knight with a lance fights a dragon while a princess flees in the dark, in a wild, stormy scene. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1555."),
("susanna-and-the-elders-tintoretto",7,1,"Susanna sits by her mirror in a garden, getting ready for a bath, while two old men spy on her from behind a hedge. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1555, and the story comes from the Bible."),
("venus-and-mars-surprised-by-vulcan",5,1,"A husband peeks under a table at his wife Venus and her lover Mars, who is hiding, while a little cupid and a dog look on. Jacopo Tintoretto painted this funny scene in about 1555, from the Greek myth about Venus and Vulcan."),
("miniature-self-portrait-anguissola-boston",1,0,"A small round painting shows a woman looking calmly out with a hint of a smile. Sofonisba Anguissola painted this tiny self-portrait in 1556, and it is only a few inches wide."),
("the-deliverance-of-arsinoe",6,1,"A queen is freed from chains by a hero, while a crowd of people and servants help her, in a dramatic scene full of twists. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1556."),
("the-librarian",9,0,"A man's face and body are made of books, with a bookmark for a nose and a curtain for a cloak. Giuseppe Arcimboldo painted it in about 1556, and it's a funny portrait of a scholar made out of the things he loves."),
("diana-and-actaeon",5,1,"The hunter Actaeon bursts into a clearing and sees the goddess Diana bathing with her nymphs, and she is about to turn him into a stag. Titian painted it in about 1557, and the red curtain and the shocked faces make it dramatic."),
("portrait-of-a-gentleman-in-a-fur",1,0,"A man in a big, thick fur coat leans on a table with a calm, intent gaze. Paolo Veronese painted this portrait in about 1558."),
("netherlandish-proverbs",4,0,"Dozens of people in a village act out proverbs: one man bangs his head on a wall, another throws money into a river, and a man tries to cut something with a knife on a roof. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted this in 1559, and over a hundred sayings are hidden in it."),
("portrait-group-with-the-artists-father-brother-and-sist",1,0,"A father, a son and a daughter stand close together, with the little boy pushing a big dog. Sofonisba Anguissola painted her family in 1559, when she was in her twenties."),
("the-fight-between-carnival-and-lent",4,0,"A fat man on a barrel with a roast pig on a spit fights a thin woman on a cart with fish and bread, in a crowded town square. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1559, and it shows the end of the party time before Lent."),
("children-s-games",4,0,"More than 200 children play about 80 games in a village street, like leapfrog, blind man's buff, rolling hoops and walking on stilts. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1560, and you can find games that are still played today."),
("christ-among-the-doctors-veronese",7,0,"A young Jesus sits in the middle of old scholars who listen carefully, with a lot of hands and books. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1560."),
("the-marriage-feast-at-cana",7,0,"A crowd of wedding guests feast under a leafy archway, with Christ at the table. It is a painting after Hieronymus Bosch, from about 1560, and the story is when Christ turned water into wine."),
("the-rape-of-europa",5,0,"A princess rides on the back of a white bull as he swims out to sea, while little cupids fly around them. Titian painted it in about 1560, and the bull was really the god Zeus in disguise. Her name is now the name of a continent."),
("the-triumph-of-death-elder",9,0,"Skeleton armies attack the living in a burnt, bare landscape, with graves, wheels and ships in the distance. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in about 1560, and no one escapes, not kings, soldiers or lovers."),
("finding-of-the-body-of-st-mark",7,0,"People find a saint's body in a dark crypt, and spirits fly out, in a deeply shadowed, deep perspective. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1562."),
("the-fall-of-the-rebel-angels",9,0,"Angels in armor fight and tumble out of heaven, and as they fall they change into monsters and fish. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1562, and the strange creatures are inspired by Hieronymus Bosch."),
("the-wedding-at-cana",7,0,"More than a hundred guests feast at a huge table, with musicians in the middle playing their instruments, and Jesus in the center. Paolo Veronese painted this giant picture in 1563, and it hangs in the Louvre, directly across from the Mona Lisa."),
("dull-gret",9,0,"A fierce woman in armor with a sword and a basket of loot marches into the mouth of hell, past burning buildings and monsters. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in about 1563, and Mad Meg is based on a Flemish folk tale."),
("last-supper",7,0,"Christ and his friends gather around a table, and servants and angels hover in the dark room, with the light of a lamp, in a very diagonal composition. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in 1563."),
("penitent-magdalene",7,0,"Mary Magdalene looks up toward heaven with tears in her eyes, with a jar and a skull nearby. Titian painted it in about 1563, and his loose, quick brushwork shows the emotion."),
("skoroposlushnitsa",7,0,"An icon, a holy painting, shows Mary as the Quick to Hear, who is thought to answer prayers fast. An unknown painter made it in the Dochiariou monastery on Mount Athos in Greece, and visitors there still pray in front of it."),
("st-mark-s-body-brought-to-venice",7,0,"Sailors carry the body of Saint Mark through a storm in a crowded square, with strong colors and diagonal lines. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in 1564, about the legend of how Saint Mark's body came to Venice."),
("the-procession-to-calvary",7,0,"Christ stumbles, carrying the cross, among a huge crowd on the way up a hill, and he is hard to spot at first. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1564, and it is full of tiny stories."),
("allegory-of-virtue-and-vice",9,0,"A young man stands between two women, one telling him to follow the path of duty and the other tempting him with pleasures. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1565."),
("christ-and-the-woman-taken-in-adultery",7,0,"Christ writes on the ground with his finger while a crowd of angry people stand around, and a woman looks down in fear. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565, in shades of gray, and it shows the story, 'Let him who is without sin cast the first stone.'"),
("crucifixion",7,0,"A huge crowd of people gather around Christ on the cross in a huge, dramatic scene with the sky growing dark. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in 1565 for the Scuola Grande di San Rocco in Venice."),
("dormition-of-the-virgin",7,0,"The apostles gather around Mary on her deathbed, while Christ stands above her holding her soul. El Greco painted it in about 1565 when he was still a young painter on the Greek island of Crete."),
("the-family-of-darius-before-alexander-veronese",6,0,"The family of a defeated king kneels before Alexander the Great, and the queen mistakenly bows to the wrong man. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1565, with sumptuous clothes and a grand palace."),
("the-gloomy-day",2,0,"Cold, dark clouds hang over a river and village in early spring, while people prune trees and hunt. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565, as one of six paintings of the months of the year."),
("the-harvesters",4,0,"Farm workers cut wheat under a hot sun, while a group sits under a tree to eat lunch, in a golden field. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565, as part of a series of the months, and it shows August."),
("the-hay-harvest-early-summer-june-july",4,0,"Peasants rake and carry hay in a green valley, with a sunny summer sky. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565 as part of the series of the months, showing June and July."),
("the-hunters-in-the-snow",4,0,"Three hunters trudge home through the snow with their dogs, while villagers skate and play on frozen ponds below. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565, and it is one of the most loved winter scenes in the world."),
("the-return-of-the-herd",2,0,"Herdsmen drive cattle home down a hillside in fall, under a stormy, golden sky, with a river and mountains beyond. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1565, as one of his six months paintings."),
("the-jurist",9,0,"A man's face is made out of a chicken, a fish and a pile of legal papers and books. Giuseppe Arcimboldo painted it in 1566, and it makes fun of lawyers."),
("the-tailor",1,0,"A tailor stands with big shears in his hand, looking up from a piece of cloth with a quiet, serious face. Giovanni Battista Moroni painted it in about 1567, and it is one of the first portraits of a working man in Italian art."),
("adoration-of-the-child",7,0,"Mary and Joseph kneel before the baby Jesus in a rundown stable, while shepherds watch from a hillside. A painter in the style of Hieronymus Bosch made this in the 1500s."),
("the-blind-leading-the-blind",9,0,"Six blind men stumble along a path, and the first has already fallen into a ditch while the others follow. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1568, and it is based on a Bible verse, and the details of their faces are painstaking."),
("the-magpie-on-the-gallows",9,0,"A magpie sits on a gallows beside a sunny valley, where peasants dance. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1568, and the magpie means gossip, and its message is that gossipy people end up on the gallows."),
("the-misanthrope",9,0,"An old man in black walks along, scowling, while a thief cuts his purse from behind him, and a tiny man sits in a glass ball. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in 1568, and the Latin text says that because the world is faithless, I go in mourning."),
("the-peasant-wedding",4,0,"Villagers at a wedding feast sit at a rough wooden table, and servants carry in bowls of porridge on a door, while a piper stands nearby. Pieter Bruegel the Elder painted it in about 1568, and the bride sits quietly under a green cloth."),
("christ-at-the-sea-of-galilee",7,0,"Christ stands on the shore and calls to his disciples in a boat, in a dark, stormy scene. This is from the circle of Tintoretto, from about 1570."),
("danae-tintoretto",5,1,"A princess lies on a bed as a shower of gold falls on her, while a maid holds a cloth to catch the coins. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1570, and the story is a Greek myth."),
("the-cook",9,0,"A man's face is made from a plate of roast meat, with his body made of a dish and a bowl. Giuseppe Arcimboldo painted it in about 1570, and if you turn the picture upside down, it becomes a plate of meat on a tray."),
("the-feast-in-the-house-of-simon-the-pharisee",7,0,"Christ sits at a long banquet table, and a woman washes his feet, in a grand hall with columns and arches. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1570."),
("the-penitent-mary-magdalene",7,0,"Mary Magdalene looks up to heaven with wet eyes, with her hands clasped and her hair spilling over her shoulder. El Greco painted it in about 1570, and he painted many versions."),
("venus-and-mars-veronese",5,1,"Mars, the god of war, sits quietly while Venus presses milk from her breast, and a cupid ties them together. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1570, and it is about how love can bring peace."),
("a-lady-in-her-bath",1,1,"A woman in a bath, looking out at us, with a nurse and a baby in the background. François Clouet painted it in about 1571, and the lady is sometimes said to be Diane de Poitiers."),
("allegory-of-the-battle-of-lepanto",6,0,"Venice's ruler kneels in the clouds before Mary while a huge naval battle rages below. Paolo Veronese painted this in 1571 to celebrate the victory over the Ottoman fleet."),
("portrait-of-giulio-clovio",1,0,"An old man in black holds a book of tiny paintings, looking out gently, with a shadowed face. El Greco painted Giulio Clovio in 1571, a master of miniature painting who was his friend."),
("the-feast-in-the-house-of-levi",7,0,"A giant feast fills a Venetian palace with servants, musicians, a dog and a drunk man. Paolo Veronese painted this in 1573, and was brought before the Inquisition for putting all these party guests in a religious scene, so he changed the title."),
("madonna-of-the-cat",7,0,"Mary sits holding the baby Jesus, while a cat looks up from the floor and the young John the Baptist teases it with a goldfinch. Federico Barocci painted it in about 1575, and the cat is very lifelike."),
("pieta",7,0,"Mary holds the dead Christ in a dark, painterly picture, with a saint kneeling and an old man at the left. Titian painted it in about 1575, as he was dying, and it was finished by Palma il Giovane."),
("the-mystic-marriage-of-st-catherine",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit in a glorious cloud of light with Saint Catherine, in a rich Venetian scene. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1575."),
("the-origin-of-the-milky-way",5,1,"The god Jupiter holds up the baby Hercules to the goddess Juno, and her milk sprays across the sky, making a path of stars. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in about 1575, and it's the Greek explanation for the Milky Way."),
("the-disrobing-of-christ",7,0,"Christ stands in his red robe, looking up, while a crowd of men and women crowd around him in a tight space. El Greco painted it in 1578 for Toledo Cathedral, and the red robe is the center of the picture."),
("madonna-of-the-people",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus, with John the Baptist, are lit from heaven while a crowd of people from the town gather below. Federico Barocci painted it in 1579, and the people include beggars, a nurse and mothers."),
("lucretia-veronese",6,0,"A Roman woman raises a dagger to her chest in a gloomy room, as she is determined to end her life to save her honor. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1580, and the story is about the start of the Roman Republic."),
("pine-trees",2,0,"Misty pine trees appear and fade into the fog on a pair of folding screens, painted in black ink. Hasegawa Tōhaku painted it in the late 1500s, and it is one of the best-known paintings in Japan."),
("the-bean-eater",4,0,"A farmer sits at a table with a bowl of beans, a loaf of bread and a glass of wine, and he looks up as if you've interrupted his meal. Annibale Carracci painted it in about 1583, and it is one of the first paintings of an ordinary working man."),
("the-fall-of-the-titans",5,1,"Huge muscular giants tumble in the air, falling from heaven in a twisting heap. Cornelis van Haarlem painted it in 1588, and he showed off his skill at painting the human body."),
("the-nobleman-with-his-hand-on-his-chest",1,0,"A man in black with a white collar and a tiny beard puts his hand on his chest, looking out with tired eyes. El Greco painted it in about 1580, and nobody knows who he was."),
("venus-and-adonis",5,1,"Venus tries to hold back the handsome Adonis, who is going out to hunt, while a little Cupid sleeps. Paolo Veronese painted it in about 1580, and the story ends with his death."),
("corpse-of-christ",7,0,"Christ's dead body lies stretched out on a slab, painted in a shocking, foreshortened view. Annibale Carracci painted it in about 1582, and Mantegna's Lamentation had inspired the shocking angle."),
("crucifixion-and-saints",7,0,"Christ hangs on a dark cross, with saints standing on both sides under a big, cloudy sky. Annibale Carracci painted it in 1583."),
("the-burial-of-the-count-of-orgaz",7,0,"Two saints in gleaming robes lower a dead nobleman into his tomb, while the noblemen of Toledo watch and a vision of heaven opens above. El Greco painted it in 1586, and it is his most famous work."),
("assumption-of-the-virgin-carracci",7,0,"The apostles look up in wonder at the empty tomb while Mary rises into the sky on a cloud of angels. Annibale Carracci painted it in about 1587."),
("saints-peter-and-paul",7,0,"Two saints stand together, one with the keys and the other with a book, in a stormy scene with strong colors. El Greco painted this in about 1587."),
("self-portrait-tintoretto",1,0,"An old man with a white beard and a gaunt face looks out of a dark background. Jacopo Tintoretto painted this self-portrait in about 1587, near the end of his life."),
("the-gardener",9,0,"A bowl of vegetables, which looks like a still life, turns into a man's face when you turn it upside down. Giuseppe Arcimboldo painted it in about 1590, and the roots, onions and peas make up the face."),
("paradise",7,0,"Hundreds of saints, angels and ordinary people swirl around in the clouds in this giant painting, which fills the whole end wall of a council hall. Jacopo Tintoretto painted it in 1588, and it is one of the biggest oil paintings in the world."),
("bacchus",5,0,"A young man in a white toga, with grapes in his hair, offers you a glass of wine, and a bowl of fruit and a pitcher stand before him. Caravaggio painted it in about 1595, and the god's face may be that of his friend or his own."),
("lady-jane-dudley-nee-grey",1,0,"A young woman in a dark dress stands with a prayer book, in a portrait said to show Lady Jane Grey. She was queen of England for only nine days in 1553, and was executed at age 16 or 17."),
("medusa-caravaggio",5,0,"Medusa's head with her hair of snakes screams in horror, painted on a round shield. Caravaggio painted it in about 1597, and the face is said to be his own, shown at the moment of being beheaded."),
("two-children-teasing-a-cat",4,0,"Two kids laugh as one pulls a cat by the tail and the cat hisses and scratches. Annibale Carracci painted this funny scene in about 1590, and it is a warning that teasing leads to scratches."),
("rudolf-ii-as-vertumnus",9,0,"The emperor's face is made of fruit, vegetables and flowers, with pears for his chin and peas for his eyelids. Giuseppe Arcimboldo painted Emperor Rudolf II as the Roman god of the seasons in 1591."),
("venus-adonis-and-cupid",5,1,"The goddess Venus and the hunter Adonis sit together as a little Cupid and hunting dogs rest nearby. Annibale Carracci painted it in about 1591."),
("resurrection-of-christ",7,0,"Christ steps out of his tomb with a banner, while soldiers lie scattered on the ground. Annibale Carracci painted this in about 1593, and his swirling cloak is full of motion."),
("boy-bitten-by-a-lizard",4,0,"A boy with a rose behind his ear jerks back, screaming in pain, as a lizard bites his finger. Caravaggio painted it in about 1594, and the quick, shocked expression is brilliantly caught."),
("boy-with-a-basket-of-fruit",1,0,"A boy in a loose white shirt holds a basket of fruit and looks over his shoulder, and the fruit is painted very realistically, with some of it going bad. Caravaggio painted it in about 1594."),
("gabrielle-d-estrees-et-une-de-ses-surs",1,1,"Two women sit in a bath, and one pinches the other's chest, while a servant sews in the background. An unknown painter made it in about 1594, and it is said to show Gabrielle d'Estrées, the favorite of King Henry IV, and her sister."),
("the-fortune-teller",4,0,"A young gypsy woman reads a boy's palm while stealing his ring with her other hand. Caravaggio painted it in about 1594, and the boy is too charmed to notice."),
("saint-peter-and-saint-paul",7,0,"Two saints stand together in a bold, tall picture, one with the keys of heaven and the other with a sword. El Greco painted it in about 1595."),
("self-portrait-as-bacchus",1,0,"A young man with a wreath of ivy leaves and a bunch of grapes looks out with a sickly, greenish tone. Caravaggio painted it in about 1595, and it is known as the Sick Bacchus, since it was painted when he had been ill."),
("the-musicians",4,0,"Four young men dressed as ancient Greeks tune their instruments, including a lute and a cornett, with sheet music on the table. Caravaggio painted it in about 1595, and he painted himself as the boy at the back."),
("the-cardsharps",4,0,"A young man studies his cards while his opponent glances over his shoulder, and another player pulls a card from behind his back. Caravaggio painted it in about 1596, and it was his first big success."),
("the-choice-of-hercules",5,0,"A young Hercules sits between two women, one offering him the easy path of pleasure and the other offering the hard path of duty. Annibale Carracci painted it in about 1596."),
("view-of-toledo",2,0,"A green city on a hill is under a dark, stormy sky, with flashes of light on its walls and the river below. El Greco painted it in about 1599, and it is one of the first great landscapes in Spanish painting."),
("nativity-barocci",7,0,"Mary, Joseph and shepherds gather around the glowing baby Jesus, while angels watch from above. Federico Barocci painted it in about 1597, and the soft pink and blue colors give it a sweet quiet."),
("saint-martin-and-the-beggar",7,0,"A young soldier on a white horse cuts his red cloak in half to share it with a poor man. El Greco painted it in about 1597, and the story is told about how Saint Martin was kind."),
("the-resurrection",7,0,"Christ rises from his tomb in a twisting swirl, while soldiers tumble around him. El Greco painted it in about 1598, and the long, stretched bodies are typical of his style."),
]
json.dump([list(r) for r in R],open("../out/old_05.json","w"),ensure_ascii=False,indent=0)
print(len(R))
